      ":question/id": "0d70558d-9878-55b8-b37b-3292e69959ea",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-129207",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th rows of $A$ are $7$, $3$, and $-7$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $7+3+(-7)=3.$"
    },
